# Economy_Simulation — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Simulation-first economies (strategy_simulation).

## 2. This document owns
- Economic model: production chains, supply/demand rules, price formation formulas.
- Simulation parameters: tick rates, elasticity constants, sink/source magnitudes.
- Stability analysis: inflation/deflation guards, intervention levers.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Resource content definitions (what resources exist) — Resource_And_Economy.
- Player-facing trade UI — UI_UX.
- Faction pricing modifiers — Faction_Design (supplies coefficients).

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Model philosophy / 2. Production chains / 3. Supply & demand / 4. Price formation / 5. Sinks & sources / 6. Stability guards / 7. Intervention levers / 8. Calibration plan / 9. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Economy_Simulation vs Resource: formulas and dynamics here; content lists there.
- Every formula's variables are owned or linked — no ghost constants.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Each chain node declares inputs, outputs and yield formula.
- Every declared guard has a trigger threshold and an action.
